WEBVTT

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:07.830
Stop the car. What's wrong?

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:08.670
I got hit.

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:09.410
What?

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:14.650
Don't be stupid. I've been watching.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.040
No one's walking.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.190
No one was there.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:19.150
That's strange.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.390
I got hit.

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:22.460
A dog or a human?

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.300
That's strange.

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:32.080
Yeah.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:15.930
This is suicide.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:23.850
I can't live any longer.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:25.380
You've been made invisible as an invisible unit.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.440
Now that I think about it, I'm invisible.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.490
They were so stupid.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.440
You and I were made to be lifeless humans.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:40.740
Nothing is possible in this world anymore.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:44.640
You say you will continue to live, but I am no longer.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:48.820
You have hope. Please live strong.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:53.550
Everyone, that's all for today at 11 a.m.

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:55.780
The mysterious suicide incident that broke out in Ginza, the center of Japan,

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:58.000
is coming to an end.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.530
In order to find out the information and cooperate with the people,

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.250
we have a message from the police officer.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.910
According to the investigation,

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:14.380
the man in the military uniform was confirmed to be a transparent man.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.240
This is due to the effect of a kind of radiation ray

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:20.800
created by the military in the past for strategic purposes.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:28.570
However, the special forces that were formed with this transparent man...

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:29.690
A special force has been deployed.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:31.190
in the northernmost part of Saipan Island.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:41.560
But the incident led to the death of at least two people,

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:46.640
who are believed to have survived in the city.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:49.590
One of them has died,

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:53.970
and the other is believed to have survived.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:59.940
If this transparent...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.980
If you find any clues about the invisible man,

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:06.530
please let the police know.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.900
Please cooperate with us.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:13.900
That's all for the news about the invisible man.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.500
This is Nihon TV.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.210
What's going on?

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:21.530
I can't believe it.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:22.930
Isn't it happening?

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:24.770
It's getting more and more serious.

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:25.900
What's going on?

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:28.050
If we get caught by the invisible man, we'll be in trouble.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:29.090
We'll be in trouble.

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:32.020
I'd like to see you for once.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:34.190
It's impossible to see what you can't see.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:36.200
Come on, let's go.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:41.970
Don't talk nonsense.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:45.670
Mariko, you have bad eyesight.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:48.210
You shouldn't go out alone.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:49.820
Don't go anywhere.

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:51.740
There's a cup of bread and an orange in it.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:57.080
Gabi, let's go out.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:59.020
No, we're not going anywhere.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:03.960
Thank you for taking care of me.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:10.880
Don't be shy.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.470
Look behind you.

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:15.970
Why?

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:17.800
It's an invisible man.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.620
How do I know?

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:21.550
I can't see him.

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:34.610
Is the director here?

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:35.450
Yes, he's here.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:46.490
Director, it wasn't good.

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:48.050
What? It wasn't good?

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:48.550
Why?

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:50.580
Dr. Nishizaka, who invented the transparent ray,

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:52.800
is certainly in pain,

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:54.360
but he died three years ago.

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:57.080
Therefore, the news in that direction is completely hopeless.

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:02.990
But I met Commander Hayakawa at the time.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:04.960
This is a photo.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:07.640
But I can't say anything concrete about it.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.540
I see.

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:15.610
Anyway, you're the witness of the incident.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:16.890
I'll give you the information about the invisible man.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:19.340
Do your best.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:20.600
Yes, sir.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.910
Send me an interview with Commander Hayakawa right away.

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:24.470
Yes, I've already done it.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:25.500
I see.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:26.740
You're really into it.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:04.810
You're Piero's uncle, aren't you?

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:06.960
Yes, I am.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.260
Even if you can't see, you can tell by the air.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:15.450
Good people, bad people, kind people.

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:17.130
They're all different.

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:20.480
Oh, I'm impressed.

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:23.720
Grandpa, you're working late again today.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:25.220
What about you?

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:28.510
I'm just going to get some fresh air.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.200
You'll buy something, won't you?

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:22.460
Oh, shadow of the world, oh lord, on the day of your death

00:09:32.236 --> 00:09:33.076
EBC.

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:02.460
to be continued ...

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:08.050
It's not easy to use a transparent man for a show.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:45.900
In the chest of my feet

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:00.590
Thanks for watching!

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:31.500
What are you doing?

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:01.900
I just wanted to take a look at the kanji.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:25.360
I'm sorry. It's all over the place.

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:28.220
No, it's not that.

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:32.280
It's all right. He's not going to lose to that guy.

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:42.680
It's that guy, isn't it? I heard it from Mai.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:56.340
It's nothing.

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:20.010
I'll give it to you!

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:44.260
Mr. Nishizaki, you said Dr. Nishizaki, the inventor of the invisible man, was your student, right?

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:46.790
Yes, that's what Nishizaki said.

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:51.100
He said it was a shock experiment done by a cyclotron.

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:54.610
I see.

00:16:57.360 --> 00:16:59.600
The experiment was a coincidence.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.680
It seems that the radiation found in the forest was the one that made the object transparent.

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:07.060
Then, after all...

00:17:07.270 --> 00:17:13.900
In other words, it is the P-33 element, the radioactive component of the forest element.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:19.900
It has a long-term continuous impact on the ultra-high speed element.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:23.220
It seems that it was discovered by chance when it was trying to see the changes in the P-33 element.

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:29.640
More...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:30.660
Could you tell me more about it?

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:34.160
Well, it's a process of absorbing the radiation.

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:39.780
It's called a hoston.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:41.720
By absorbing the hoston,

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:44.640
we can pass through 100% of the gas line.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:48.390
That means we can also make humans transparent.

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:55.460
But we can't restore it.

00:17:56.020 --> 00:17:57.840
Then, what about the sales of Keiba Castle

00:17:57.840 --> 00:17:59.480
and Nagayama's case?

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.420
The suspect is a member of the special forces.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:04.900
So the police chief has to be taken care of.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:08.020
The police chief will be fined 20 million yen if he is arrested.

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:09.580
What is the police chief's plan?

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:11.890
Is it true that the law enforcement department is summoning police officers?

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:15.760
I don't know. Please forgive us.

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:28.140
I will take responsibility for that.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:34.990
I have no choice but to answer your questions.

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:48.800
I'm not asking for your responsibility.

00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:54.570
I don't care how much I cut your nose, but this is not the time for that.

00:18:54.790 --> 00:18:57.600
I'm asking whether the invisible man will be caught or not.

00:19:00.920 --> 00:19:01.920
I'll catch him.

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:04.730
You don't have to say such a big thing.

00:19:06.800 --> 00:19:10.040
Tomin is being attacked every day for a reason no one else knows.

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:16.440
If this happens, the train will be blown up,

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:20.290
or a dynamite will be set on a large facility in Koshu.

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:23.920
Even if you do that, you won't be seen, so you won't know.

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:27.110
I don't know if he's here or not.

00:19:27.210 --> 00:19:29.760
You're... You're...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:30.460
I'm going to shoot you.

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:04.360
What's wrong? You must be lonely without me.

00:20:07.070 --> 00:20:11.040
You're working so hard to make me happy.

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:19.860
That's right. I've been thinking about it.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:22.520
I want to buy you something so you don't get bored.

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:25.430
What do you want?

00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:27.360
What?

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:29.240
Why?

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:33.400
You're poor, aren't you?

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:35.370
No, I'm not.

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:36.580
I'm rich.

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:41.550
Actually, I want an orgel.

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:43.340
An orgel?

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:45.760
I had one.

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:48.920
I bought it to celebrate my parents' wedding.

00:20:50.380 --> 00:20:54.120
But it got burned in the war and died.

00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:56.940
I see.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:04.290
When I hear that, I think of my father and mother very much.

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:08.360
I don't have any of that these days, so I feel like I'm going to forget.

00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:12.750
When I open the door, I hear a nostalgic Jenny.

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:19.960
Hey, old man, isn't your sister still awake?

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:22.900
The curtain is closed, so she's not here yet.

00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:29.340
Go home. Dai-chan, you're not going anywhere.

00:21:30.920 --> 00:21:33.450
I told you I was going to use Master's money today.

00:21:33.970 --> 00:21:35.390
I'm talking about my father.

00:21:35.910 --> 00:21:39.980
If that's the case, you should have refused.

00:21:40.420 --> 00:21:42.100
Tell Yajima that.

00:21:42.600 --> 00:21:44.280
Is that all right?

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:46.400
If I stand up to Master too much...

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:47.080
Leave it alone.

00:21:47.180 --> 00:21:49.300
You're using such a good old man.

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:51.960
I'm helping him.

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:54.230
This money will cure that girl's eyes.

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:56.880
Is that what you're going to do?

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:57.320
Yes.

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:00.650
I can't help it.

00:22:00.810 --> 00:22:10.820
Miss, is Grandpa home?

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:13.400
He hasn't come home yet.

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:13.880
Hmm?

00:22:14.130 --> 00:22:14.760
Do you need anything?

00:22:16.030 --> 00:22:16.870
No, thanks.

00:22:17.110 --> 00:22:19.220
You can tell Master.

00:22:19.860 --> 00:22:20.950
He said he didn't want to.

00:22:21.090 --> 00:22:21.730
No problem.

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:24.140
Hmm, I see.

00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:24.640
Bye.

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:38.010
Good morning, Mari.

00:22:38.490 --> 00:22:39.820
Who is this woman?

00:22:41.950 --> 00:22:45.100
You don't know her.

00:22:45.320 --> 00:22:45.740
Really?

00:22:48.230 --> 00:22:50.600
Soon, you'll be able to see her face.

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:53.770
Soon?

00:22:55.840 --> 00:22:59.360
Soon, you'll be able to make money.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:03.370
Then I'll be hospitalized for eye surgery.

00:23:33.130 --> 00:23:34.810
It doesn't matter how expensive it is, but can't you order it?

00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:36.190
It's a nostalgic jelly.

00:23:36.730 --> 00:23:37.430
That's right.

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:39.410
Let's order it here.

00:23:39.590 --> 00:23:40.260
For Christmas.

00:23:40.700 --> 00:23:41.540
Thank you very much.

00:23:41.780 --> 00:23:42.680
Yes, thank you very much.

00:23:42.900 --> 00:23:48.080
What's wrong?

00:23:48.300 --> 00:23:50.060
It's no good.

00:23:50.380 --> 00:23:51.300
It's like he's using a spider.

00:23:51.960 --> 00:23:52.620
Of course not.

00:23:52.980 --> 00:23:54.480
He's a transparent person.

00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:56.900
Well, I'll do it little by little.

00:23:57.100 --> 00:23:57.460
Chief.

00:24:00.410 --> 00:24:01.130
What do you think transparent people do?

00:24:03.940 --> 00:24:06.440
They eat, don't they?

00:24:06.600 --> 00:24:08.000
Of course they do.

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:10.420
Then, in order to eat it,

00:24:10.620 --> 00:24:12.480
we need to be able to see.

00:24:15.530 --> 00:24:17.540
I see.

00:24:20.860 --> 00:24:21.840
Rather than looking for something invisible,

00:24:22.540 --> 00:24:23.530
shouldn't we look for something visible?

00:24:24.670 --> 00:24:26.720
Do you have any idea?

00:24:27.220 --> 00:24:29.000
No, I'm not sure yet.

00:24:36.200 --> 00:24:40.500
It would be great if you could become a transparent man and sneak into a woman's bath.

00:24:41.650 --> 00:24:43.740
The trip would be ridiculous.

00:24:44.420 --> 00:24:45.540
Shut up.

00:24:45.820 --> 00:24:46.740
I'm not talking about a transparent man.

00:24:47.800 --> 00:24:49.530
Hey, O-chan.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.870
What? Where is it?

00:25:01.950 --> 00:25:03.120
It's a metal shop.

00:25:03.460 --> 00:25:04.930
I'll take care of it.

00:25:14.760 --> 00:25:18.420
How is it?

00:25:18.900 --> 00:25:21.030
Is it true that humans are invisible?

00:25:21.270 --> 00:25:22.210
Yes, it seems so.

00:25:23.280 --> 00:25:24.520
What's the news?

00:25:25.160 --> 00:25:27.620
I heard that Piero came here this afternoon.

00:25:27.720 --> 00:25:28.800
That's strange.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.540
He ordered a Golgol and went to see the shop.

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:35.410
Thank you very much.

00:25:35.690 --> 00:25:40.720
This is Pier 3-1, isn't it?

00:25:40.780 --> 00:25:42.660
Yes, it is.

00:25:42.860 --> 00:25:47.840
This is Nanjo Takamitsu.

00:25:48.220 --> 00:25:50.450
The address is Hewaso apartment in Tsukiji-katabachi.

00:25:50.510 --> 00:25:53.100
Thank you very much.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:02.100
Well, Nanjo said she wanted some hot water.

00:26:04.060 --> 00:26:05.800
I think she came around 11 last night.

00:26:06.660 --> 00:26:08.320
Yes, around 11.

00:26:08.600 --> 00:26:09.620
Yes, that's right.

00:26:10.340 --> 00:26:12.360
I'm in Nanjo's bedroom.

00:26:13.220 --> 00:26:15.710
I've been in her room since then.

00:26:15.950 --> 00:26:17.060
Is that so?

00:26:17.490 --> 00:26:19.010
Thank you.

00:26:49.930 --> 00:26:51.090
I'm going to make a sandwich out of this.

00:28:00.030 --> 00:28:00.890
What do you think, old man?

00:28:01.090 --> 00:28:05.320
Do you want to fix your daughter's life with that 100,000 yen?

00:28:05.680 --> 00:28:10.040
I'm not forcing you to do anything.

00:28:10.360 --> 00:28:12.610
If you could lend me some money, I'd be happy to do that.

00:28:14.690 --> 00:28:16.780
Hey, old man, I'm not going to bother you.

00:28:17.760 --> 00:28:19.320
What's wrong with you?

00:28:20.070 --> 00:28:22.000
You're keeping a secret from me.

00:28:22.420 --> 00:28:25.020
If you say you don't want to do it, I'll have to do it myself.

00:28:56.430 --> 00:28:56.970
He said to be careful.

00:29:10.400 --> 00:29:13.350
Put the motorboat on the other side of the bridge.

00:29:14.550 --> 00:29:16.590
The Mishima truck is waiting here.

00:29:16.610 --> 00:29:18.480
Yes, sir.

00:29:18.640 --> 00:29:26.480
Don't let anyone get away.

00:29:35.400 --> 00:29:37.780
Michio, it's your turn.

00:30:00.124 --> 00:30:01.204
My God.

00:31:01.830 --> 00:31:29.600
I'd like you to wait here for a while.

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:30.360
What?

00:32:39.080 --> 00:32:45.920
It's me. Thank you.

00:33:30.670 --> 00:33:30.850
Hello, uncle.

00:33:31.660 --> 00:33:40.270
Hello, uncle.

00:33:40.520 --> 00:33:41.000
Hello, uncle.

00:33:41.000 --> 00:33:41.080
Hello.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:01.240
Please, I beg you.

00:34:21.820 --> 00:34:24.240
You still don't understand?

00:34:24.540 --> 00:34:25.310
I'm sorry.

00:34:25.570 --> 00:34:27.640
I can't believe I killed such a good old man.

00:34:28.260 --> 00:34:28.700
Me neither.

00:34:32.430 --> 00:34:35.150
I need.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:01.280
You're trying to trick me, aren't you?

00:36:01.280 --> 00:36:02.280
What are you doing?

00:36:02.520 --> 00:36:05.040
Please wait. I'm a journalist.

00:36:05.420 --> 00:36:05.820
What?

00:36:07.910 --> 00:36:11.410
I'm sorry.

00:36:11.610 --> 00:36:14.280
I just wanted to know.

00:36:14.500 --> 00:36:14.980
That's all.

00:36:15.200 --> 00:36:15.920
You wanted to know?

00:36:16.040 --> 00:36:17.550
My identity as a transparent man?

00:36:32.230 --> 00:36:33.310
I know.

00:36:35.900 --> 00:36:36.240
What?

00:36:36.890 --> 00:36:39.730
You're the one who attacked the jewellery store and killed Shimagura.

00:36:41.320 --> 00:36:45.880
I'm a journalist called Komatsu.

00:36:45.880 --> 00:36:47.490
I want to make the right report.

00:36:47.910 --> 00:36:48.760
That's all.

00:36:48.980 --> 00:36:49.900
Please believe me.

00:36:50.180 --> 00:36:51.780
I see.

00:36:52.160 --> 00:36:54.830
I was so excited.

00:36:55.610 --> 00:36:57.710
No, I'm sorry.

00:37:00.800 --> 00:37:04.910
Mr. Komatsu, you are the first person who believed in me.

00:37:05.470 --> 00:37:07.850
Please listen to me.

00:37:09.370 --> 00:37:14.280
I am a man who was robbed by the army of my identity as a human.

00:37:14.440 --> 00:37:20.980
When I return to Japan, the beautiful soil of Japan is bleeding.

00:37:21.560 --> 00:37:27.300
Even if I go to see my mother, I can't find my identity.

00:37:27.640 --> 00:37:29.540
What should I do?

00:37:31.310 --> 00:37:32.880
My mother died of illness.

00:37:33.080 --> 00:37:38.200
She passed away.

00:37:38.760 --> 00:37:43.020
I thought I was going to die like a voice actor.

00:37:44.480 --> 00:37:48.570
But I could do something.

00:37:49.130 --> 00:37:50.280
My mother was a Christian.

00:37:50.920 --> 00:37:52.270
She taught me.

00:37:52.610 --> 00:37:54.570
She believed in me.

00:37:54.670 --> 00:37:56.590
She took care of me.

00:37:56.990 --> 00:37:58.950
She didn't disturb me.

00:38:00.510 --> 00:38:02.260
That's how I came to life, as a pianist.

00:38:08.760 --> 00:38:11.670
What can I say, Mr. Nanjo?

00:38:11.670 --> 00:38:18.170
But I'd like to ask you for your help.

00:38:18.270 --> 00:38:19.980
Thank you.

00:38:21.240 --> 00:38:25.030
But please don't tell anyone about me.

00:38:25.090 --> 00:38:29.460
I've worked as a pianist for many years.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:30.320
until we capture the young dog.

00:38:32.140 --> 00:38:35.210
I understand. Please let me help you.

00:38:35.510 --> 00:38:36.750
Thank you.

00:38:36.750 --> 00:38:42.620
Mr. Komatsu, let me show you this one thing

00:38:42.620 --> 00:38:43.040
that was created by the Kunkoku family.

00:39:42.480 --> 00:39:45.930
This is me. I'll use this to get the gang out of here.

00:40:09.560 --> 00:40:10.060
Nice to meet you.

00:40:10.160 --> 00:40:12.500
About the invisible man last night.

00:40:12.900 --> 00:40:13.760
How many people were there?

00:40:13.940 --> 00:40:16.290
Oh, I see.

00:40:16.470 --> 00:40:18.120
I think it was four people.

00:40:18.460 --> 00:40:18.960
Who were they?

00:40:19.490 --> 00:40:23.020
They were all in the fire chief's office.

00:40:24.080 --> 00:40:25.000
Oh, really?

00:40:25.510 --> 00:40:26.780
Well, what do you think?

00:40:27.480 --> 00:40:27.760
No.

00:40:36.490 --> 00:40:37.540
Sir, are you all right?

00:40:37.700 --> 00:40:38.600
Sir, are you all right?

00:40:38.940 --> 00:40:40.340
Sir, are you all right?

00:40:40.780 --> 00:40:56.880
The person who attacked me and the person who attacked the jewelry store are the same person.

00:40:57.080 --> 00:40:59.600
The one who attacked Tokaimaru at the police station...

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:01.160
He's probably the same guy, isn't he?

00:41:01.160 --> 00:41:02.030
Yes, he is.

00:41:02.030 --> 00:41:03.810
He's planning to use my name.

00:41:04.350 --> 00:41:04.850
He must be a gangster.

00:41:05.750 --> 00:41:09.480
Is there something wrong with him?

00:41:10.220 --> 00:41:11.040
I don't know.

00:41:11.440 --> 00:41:13.970
Oh, I see.

00:41:14.010 --> 00:41:14.750
Could it be...

00:41:14.750 --> 00:41:16.680
Is there something wrong with him?

00:41:16.680 --> 00:41:16.940
Yes.

00:41:17.600 --> 00:41:20.240
The old man who was killed in Tokoban

00:41:20.240 --> 00:41:23.310
said he could make 100,000 yen soon.

00:41:24.920 --> 00:41:26.600
Maybe that 100,000 yen is the reason

00:41:26.600 --> 00:41:27.760
why he was killed.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:30.660
That's a big deal.

00:41:31.140 --> 00:41:35.720
I'll look into it and contact you if I find out.

00:41:35.720 --> 00:41:38.510
Please do. I'll wait in the car.

00:41:40.120 --> 00:41:40.380
Okay.

00:41:41.410 --> 00:41:42.130
Be careful.

00:42:04.320 --> 00:42:05.500
It's your birthday, isn't it?

00:42:05.500 --> 00:42:07.340
Yes, it is, Mari-chan.

00:42:07.990 --> 00:42:09.330
It's Christmas in three days.

00:42:09.490 --> 00:42:12.230
That's why I'm keeping an eye on you.

00:42:12.530 --> 00:42:15.210
And I'm going to give you a present.

00:42:15.830 --> 00:42:16.160
I see.

00:42:16.400 --> 00:42:18.460
I promised you the Orgol the other day.

00:42:18.640 --> 00:42:20.730
I'm sure you'll make it by Christmas.

00:42:21.760 --> 00:42:22.160
Really?

00:42:22.900 --> 00:42:23.700
I think so.

00:42:24.160 --> 00:42:26.680
But there's something I'd like to ask you.

00:42:26.960 --> 00:42:28.640
What is it?

00:42:28.980 --> 00:42:29.320
Grandpa.

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:32.760
You said you'd be able to save 100,000 yen soon, didn't you?

00:42:32.780 --> 00:42:33.600
Yes, I did.

00:42:34.150 --> 00:42:36.160
Would you show me your savings account?

00:42:37.520 --> 00:42:37.880
Sure.

00:42:39.060 --> 00:42:55.140
I knew it.

00:42:55.500 --> 00:42:58.520
Did you?

00:42:58.640 --> 00:42:58.980
No.

00:43:00.060 --> 00:43:04.570
It's nothing. Hey Mari, did you see any strange people when you came to visit your grandpa?

00:43:06.190 --> 00:43:12.500
I did. I only have a map.

00:43:13.410 --> 00:43:14.870
What kind of people were they?

00:43:16.140 --> 00:43:21.880
Well, there was a person who asked me if my grandpa was in the room where my sister was staying.

00:43:22.570 --> 00:43:24.460
He seemed to be a very unpleasant person.

00:43:25.230 --> 00:43:25.910
And then?

00:43:26.400 --> 00:43:29.580
Later, when I went to visit my grandpa, he was wearing a cabaret.

00:43:30.600 --> 00:43:32.300
What? Cabaret?

00:43:32.500 --> 00:43:35.680
No, thank you.

00:43:35.880 --> 00:43:39.100
Are you going home?

00:43:39.240 --> 00:43:39.620
Yes.

00:43:40.010 --> 00:43:40.880
I have a job.

00:43:41.260 --> 00:43:42.480
I'll be back soon.

00:44:06.970 --> 00:44:08.810
Hello, is this Choyu Shimbun?

00:44:09.090 --> 00:44:12.280
I'd like to speak to Mr. Komatsu.

00:44:12.340 --> 00:44:17.080
Mr. Komatsu, this is Nanjo.

00:44:17.320 --> 00:44:22.590
I'd like to see you, but I'm waiting for you with my black hand.

00:44:23.410 --> 00:44:25.370
See you.

00:45:05.210 --> 00:45:08.700
What's going on?

00:45:08.940 --> 00:45:10.460
Someone hit me.

00:45:10.680 --> 00:45:13.400
Don't say that.

00:45:13.480 --> 00:45:14.140
It's not a big deal.

00:45:14.440 --> 00:45:15.610
But...

00:45:15.920 --> 00:45:28.960
Do you really not want to?

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:32.450
Then why did you go to Shiba-Ura last night?

00:45:34.600 --> 00:45:36.440
You're the only one who knows about Shiba-Ura.

00:45:36.480 --> 00:45:40.420
Why did you put it on?

00:45:40.560 --> 00:45:43.380
Because I was worried about my grandfather.

00:45:43.840 --> 00:45:47.380
You didn't mean to get in the way of our work, did you?

00:45:48.990 --> 00:45:55.300
If we get caught, we'll have to eat stinky rice.

00:46:36.430 --> 00:46:37.910
I think it's better to listen to the master.

00:46:38.870 --> 00:46:49.910
You really don't want to, do you?

00:46:51.430 --> 00:46:51.990
Well, then, I can't help it.

00:47:16.670 --> 00:47:17.010
You know what I'm saying, right?

00:47:18.980 --> 00:47:20.060
I'm not going to die.

00:47:21.580 --> 00:47:22.220
You know what I'm saying, right?

00:47:23.100 --> 00:47:24.400
You're my friend of mine.

00:47:26.010 --> 00:47:27.720
I'll send you this to you, right?

00:47:30.700 --> 00:47:33.320
This is the last one. Let's go.

00:47:33.600 --> 00:47:44.180
Thank you.

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:02.430
The cup fell on the floor and broke into pieces.

00:48:02.510 --> 00:48:04.360
It must be a transparent person.

00:48:04.740 --> 00:48:07.080
Don't be silly.

00:48:09.020 --> 00:48:10.210
I'm the one who hit it.

00:48:31.400 --> 00:48:31.720
Thank you very much.

00:49:07.230 --> 00:49:08.910
I'll do a minute away, man.

00:50:02.460 --> 00:50:15.620
It's Gunan-jo, Pierrot and Bunai.

00:50:15.660 --> 00:50:17.420
They're being dragged into this.

00:50:17.660 --> 00:50:18.590
Run away.

00:50:20.960 --> 00:50:25.940
What's wrong, Tashio?

00:50:26.180 --> 00:50:27.380
I want to save you.

00:50:27.480 --> 00:50:28.880
That's all I want.

00:50:29.530 --> 00:50:29.850
Believe me.

00:50:31.150 --> 00:50:35.820
Please wait for me at the music hall in Shibuya.

00:50:36.080 --> 00:50:39.320
I have something to tell you.

00:51:42.120 --> 00:51:53.000
Thank you for coming.

00:52:00.090 --> 00:52:13.550
You must be surprised. I'm a clear-minded man, but I didn't want to be known only by you.

00:52:13.670 --> 00:52:25.490
It can't be helped. Michio-san, you have to get out of your current life.

00:52:33.580 --> 00:52:37.160
Is it strange for me, an invisible man, to say such a thing?

00:52:37.520 --> 00:52:40.780
Is it true?

00:52:41.160 --> 00:52:47.380
I'm just using your name.

00:52:48.200 --> 00:52:51.320
Thank you.

00:52:51.460 --> 00:52:55.060
Well, you understand what I'm saying, don't you?

00:52:55.060 --> 00:52:58.940
Yes, but...

00:53:00.350 --> 00:53:01.430
I don't know what to do anymore.

00:53:01.710 --> 00:53:05.670
When I'm worried, I'm trapped in a trap.

00:53:06.410 --> 00:53:07.280
It's not like that.

00:53:07.460 --> 00:53:09.580
If you're worried about that,

00:53:09.580 --> 00:53:18.880
Ichiya, we can't help each other and live together.

00:53:19.440 --> 00:53:25.110
What I'm saying is,

00:53:25.130 --> 00:53:28.600
it's not like we're dating or in love.

00:53:30.730 --> 00:53:31.270
I don't know what to say.

00:53:31.820 --> 00:53:35.490
Nanjou, why can't we go on a trip around the world?

00:53:36.660 --> 00:53:37.160
Why?

00:53:37.500 --> 00:53:40.370
Because we're all the same.

00:53:40.750 --> 00:53:43.400
No, we're all the same.

00:53:43.400 --> 00:53:45.560
Nanjou...

00:54:04.540 --> 00:54:07.880
You're lucky to have shown yourself.

00:54:09.000 --> 00:54:12.000
But you're still a useless man.

00:54:12.260 --> 00:54:14.110
I want you to come with me.

00:54:33.390 --> 00:54:41.940
Are you still in your fifties?

00:54:42.220 --> 00:54:45.520
Do you really not want to be our friends?

00:55:02.590 --> 00:55:05.690
Ken, throw this away in Ginza.

00:55:06.230 --> 00:55:06.490
What?

00:55:07.440 --> 00:55:10.210
A car is going to pull it out.

00:55:10.210 --> 00:55:13.540
If a real, transparent human body comes out,

00:55:13.620 --> 00:55:16.860
everyone will come after it.

00:55:16.920 --> 00:55:18.280
I see.

00:55:20.960 --> 00:55:21.920
Make sure it has eyes.

00:55:22.540 --> 00:55:25.140
Find a station wagon.

00:55:25.500 --> 00:55:26.350
Yes, sir.

00:55:32.200 --> 00:55:33.000
Take his clothes off.

00:55:33.180 --> 00:55:34.070
Yes, sir.

00:55:34.070 --> 00:55:45.160
He's a bad guy.

00:55:54.560 --> 00:55:55.340
Anpei.

00:55:55.670 --> 00:55:56.910
Take his clothes off.

00:55:57.170 --> 00:55:57.530
What?

00:55:57.980 --> 00:55:58.460
Are you serious?

00:55:58.800 --> 00:55:59.660
It's not enough.

00:56:00.280 --> 00:56:01.080
Wipe your hands and walk.

00:56:35.690 --> 00:56:37.350
Hey, open the door if you see the fourth one.

00:56:38.650 --> 00:56:39.010
Yes, sir.

00:57:25.960 --> 00:57:28.780
Mr. Tatsuo, what about Shibawara no Fushio?

00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:32.580
No, it's fine. We have the evidence.

00:57:33.120 --> 00:57:34.920
The culprit is related to the ship.

00:57:36.220 --> 00:57:38.420
Komatsu has the evidence.

00:57:39.370 --> 00:57:40.430
Thank you.

00:57:41.890 --> 00:57:42.810
You're right.

00:57:43.830 --> 00:57:48.190
No matter how hard you try, the police won't let you off.

00:58:00.120 --> 00:58:01.850
Master, it went well.

00:58:01.990 --> 00:58:03.240
I see.

00:58:04.050 --> 00:58:04.370
Drink up.

00:58:05.650 --> 00:58:09.380
Ginza is in trouble now.

00:58:10.810 --> 00:58:14.140
We're relieved now.

00:58:15.220 --> 00:58:17.790
It was a little rough this time.

00:58:18.090 --> 00:58:20.640
It's a good time to take a breath.

00:58:21.360 --> 00:58:22.160
Drink up.

00:58:32.332 --> 00:58:32.832
Oh!

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:29.980
Thank you.

00:59:37.676 --> 00:59:39.016
I'll kill you!

01:01:03.930 --> 01:01:06.650
I can't get it.

01:05:02.040 --> 01:05:02.080
Thank you.

01:06:05.436 --> 01:06:06.436
Got it?

01:06:06.524 --> 01:06:07.524
Shut up!

01:06:08.252 --> 01:06:10.212
I'll make Tokyo my home!

01:06:14.108 --> 01:06:15.108
Stop it!

01:06:15.164 --> 01:06:16.164
Get out of here!

01:08:30.190 --> 01:08:36.730
I'm sorry.

01:08:36.890 --> 01:08:46.720
It's okay.

01:08:49.770 --> 01:08:56.130
I don't have anything to say.

01:09:13.310 --> 01:09:17.110
I hear a bell. I wonder if Uncle Pari brought it.

01:09:30.340 --> 01:09:30.460
Thank you.

01:10:00.320 --> 01:10:00.580
Thank you.
